WEBVTT

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.450
It seems to have been a young woman...

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.910
Many of her bones have been crushed.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.080
This cannot possibly be a normal assault.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.950
Also, this was found nearby.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.450
We need to find out who she was first.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.120
She would never have appeared
if it wasn't for this endless rain.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.000
Oh, yeah, have you eaten
with the Helmsmen?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.830
I have. Is there a problem?

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:53.250
Were they to your liking?

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.330
Thus, the word <i>la Terreur</i> , coined by
the Jacobins after the French Revolution,

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:55.450
became the origin for the word "terrorism."

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:02.370
Robespierre of the Jacobins Club claimed
that virtue without terror was powerless.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.700
That's all for today.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.950
Annie!

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.450
Our regular spot after this.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.540
You're coming right? For sure!

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.750
Of course, I will!

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.700
Oh, he's so obvious.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.870
He was looking at you again, Annie.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.370
Yeah. So creepy!

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.080
He drew her again!

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.870
S-Stop it!

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.910
No! No! No! He's good, but so creepy!

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.200
So this is how you see her.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.080
It's overflowing with love. Right, Annie?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.910
Th-That's just because you happen...

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.250
A-Annabella, you were just
in my line of sight!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.410
I just happened to be
sketching that accessory. Yeah.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.580
That's it. That's all!

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.540
Wh-What?

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.580
Come with us.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.910
Just kidding. Never mind.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.410
That was so mean, Annie!

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.950
Did you see his face?!

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.450
He definitely wanted to come!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.790
I'll go get some napkins.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.500
Thanks, Annie!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.120
How do you keep it up?
Even though you can't taste it.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:49.370
It's practice for when I become human.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.580
That aside, it's rare to see <i>you</i> in Upper.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.080
We're having a proxy war.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.290
--Hey! Over here!
--There he is! You're late!

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.870
Bodyguarding them like usual, huh?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.910
She's looking at us.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.200
--Yeah...
--Wow, such a beauty!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.290
She has an aura about her...

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.040
You're alive!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.330
Huh? Who are you?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.790
Um, miss? I think you have the wrong girl.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.330
Her name is Annabella.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.620
Annabella?

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:25.580
Yes.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.040
It's me, Elaine Heiding.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.000
We went to Arc High together.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.910
Arc High is a famous school!

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.910
More like a school for young ladies!

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.040
Wait. Wait.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.000
Miss, didn't you graduate from
high school a long time ago?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.450
That's true...

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:44.410
But that hair accessory looks just like
the one Mary made by hand.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.910
And that face... You look just like Mary.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.410
In other words,
your classmate was named Mary?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.540
--Yes.
--No way!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.120
We're still in our teens!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.540
How old are you, miss?

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.540
Twenty-seven...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.580
Ten years ago! No way! No way! No way!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.540
You're right...

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.000
Um, that accessory...

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.330
May I know where you bought it?

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.580
Good job, Belo!

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:14.540
All right!

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.700
Oh, I bought this at the flea market...

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.660
So I don't remember it well.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.870
I see. If you remember anything,
please contact me, Annabella.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.120
Yes.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.790
We've identified the victim.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:33.080
Mary Russell. She went missing at 17.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:36.250
The state of her bones
sets her death about 10 years go.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.950
Her parents had submitted
a missing persons report.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:43.790
That was pretty fast for our
forensics department. And the phone?

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.200
Data salvage was impossible.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.950
Can't be helped. Let's go to Upper.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:54.830
But why was a lady from Upper
sleeping in a place like this for 10 years?

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.160
Hopefully it won't become a problem.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.700
The origin of our faces.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.540
I wonder how they're doing now.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:09.620
Huh, Bem?

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.370
Bela, forget it. You are you.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.450
You're cold sometimes, Bem.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.700
Hey, were you guys listening to me?

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:29.000
Hi, Elaine. What's wrong? Elaine?

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.580
Where is your husband?

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.700
Work, like usual.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:33.950
Thank goodness.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.660
I wanted to show something just to you.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:38.950
What?

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:42.580
No way? Where did you see this?!

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.540
I saw this girl at the mall.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.370
She called herself Annabella.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.500
Hey, this accessory... On that day...

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.000
I thought about it for a long time.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.790
Perhaps Mary is back.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.580
Perhaps she's come to get revenge.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.080
Stop it!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.950
Mary was a part of Dominic's group.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:10.700
If I remember, Mary had stolen
Dominque's accessory or something.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.700
After the theft, everyone ignored Mary.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:12.410
There were a lot of rumors.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.080
They said she was no good.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.660
The reason? Who knows? I didn't know.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.080
Elaine was the one who said so.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.790
Elaine was the one closest to Mary.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.660
I heard Elaine was the one who calmed
Dominic during the theft incident.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:28.330
No, Elaine was more of a problem.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:29.660
She was a liar.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:32.750
Even though she was a commoner,
she always acted like she had money.

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.790
Elaine wasn't a liar.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:37.750
She was a victim of bad rumors.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.330
Good women are often used
as the source of bad rumors.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:45.660
Lies. Lies. Elaine always said terrible
things about Mary and Dominque.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.250
Only the actual girls didn't know.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:50.450
If you meet Elaine, be careful
if she says these words.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.620
"I wish I met you sooner."

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.870
I am getting more and more confused.

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:58.000
Where does the truth lie?

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.450
Elaine Heiding bothers me.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.910
Everyone keeps saying opposite things.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.750
Dominic is referring to Dominic Vali.

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:08.040
She is the daughter of a wealthy family.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.080
Her husband, Mr. Vali,
is an elite in the business world.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.750
It seems Elaine's husband also
works at Mr. Vali's company.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.950
So Elaine is lower in status.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.080
Is that so?

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.580
Yeah, that's how it is.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.750
Hey. Did you wait long?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.250
Please let me go.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:34.000
This uniform. Aren't you from Cent Joseph?

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.660
I really like girls from there.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.500
Please stop.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.790
Oh. You want a bit of spending money?

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.870
Come play with us.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:46.790
Please move. I will call the police.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:47.870
Go ahead and try.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.580
It's so cute how hard she tries!

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:55.250
Just my type. I love the fierce ones.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.250
Annabella

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.200
Shit!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.120
Are you all right? That was dangerous.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.910
Yes. Thank you!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.410
I'm so happy that you contacted me.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.000
I wanted to meet with you, too.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.330
You're not wearing that accessory?

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.830
I don't wear it every day.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.950
It depends on my feeling that day.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:23.700
I see. Mary wore it every day,
saying that it was the best one she made.

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.540
Um, your phone...

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:29.500
It's fine. I will call them back later.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.870
You are the most important
to me right now.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:37.040
Heiding isn't answering.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.370
Try calling Dominique Vali.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:43.700
I couldn't stop thinking about
the person you called Mary, after that.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.250
She was a good girl.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.040
A very honest and good girl.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.160
Her smile was so beautiful.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:55.000
She overflowed with blinding confidence
whenever she talked about her dream.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.370
Dream...

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.330
Yes.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:01.950
She wanted to become a jewelry
designer when she grew up.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:05.830
That's why she always wore
the accessories she made herself.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:09.660
But our friend, a lady named Dominic,

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.500
had her accessory stolen one time...

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:16.950
She suspected Mary, but I jumped in
to reconcile the two of them.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.500
Then, Dominic gave Mary a condition.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:25.910
If Mary won a test of bravery by going
to the Outside, they would be friends again.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.750
Everyone was against it.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.910
But no one could go against Dominic.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:35.370
She was a powerful lady... No, a queen.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.790
Mary Russell, you say?

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.410
You knew her.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.830
She was in your class in high school.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.910
I believe she went missing?

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.370
Yes. What about it?

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:50.950
We found her body.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:54.160
We'd like to speak with you
about Mary Russell.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.410
Yes, there is something I wish to discuss.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:59.080
No, not on the phone...

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:05.950
Dominic told us we should return to Upper
after seeing Mary cross the bridge.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.750
We couldn't do anything.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.660
If we went against Dominic,
we would be the next ones ignored.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:22.540
I think that Dominic lied about
her accessory being stolen.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.750
Dominic actually hated Mary and me.

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.830
She considered us lower ranking commoners.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.080
That's terrible.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:35.120
That's why she was left Outside?

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.620
I'm sick of all these terrible memories.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.790
I wanted to show you this.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:45.000
This is something Mary once made
for me as proof of our friendship.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.080
There is only one in the world.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:48.290
It's beautiful...

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.870
I want to give it to you. Try it on.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.450
I wish I met you sooner.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:04.790
Please tell me more about Mary.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.160
I want to know more!

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.830
She's always thought about Mary.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:16.160
Maybe I should tell her the truth...

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.410
Annie!

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.500
Wait! What's wrong?!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.500
Did something happen?

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:41.000
You shouldn't go past this point today.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.290
Especially if you treasure
the girl with that face.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.410
I'm going because I treasure her.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.580
Elaine?

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:06.950
I can't believe it. You're really Mary...

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.040
Who are you?

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.750
Mary, do you remember me?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:19.290
You really were the one who
stole that accessory from me.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.250
Dominic Vali?!

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.290
The way you said my name
sounds so intentional.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.160
No, it wasn't me!

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.950
I received this from Elaine.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.750
She told me Mary made it by hand!

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:30.370
Elaine said that?

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.000
Where is Elaine?

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.160
Did she meet the same fate as Mary?!

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:35.870
You were the one who called me here.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.330
I came because Elaine contacted me.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:42.910
She told me you were going to
kill her just like you killed Mary.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:02.080
First shot. Strike!

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.950
Little lady. I've seen your face before.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.870
It's the face of Mary,
who you murdered 10 years ago!

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:16.120
Yeah. It was a name like that...

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.410
So she wants me to kill you again!

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:21.200
She was crying... For help.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:28.160
Second shot! Going for a double!

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.500
G-Gutterball?!

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.120
She was crying!

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:52.540
What the hell are you?!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.830
Did you become a monster after I killed you?!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.290
Shut up!

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.450
You're the monsters here!

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:01.410
I'm gonna get my highest score with you!

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.620
Shots three and four are double-handed!

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:07.120
Release!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:18.330
So creepy!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.000
Shot five! I'll be the strike!

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.910
This one never misses!

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:32.080
Striking out!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.750
You bitch!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:49.620
Both 10 years ago and now.
Who asked you to do this?

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:50.950
Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:52.540
I was just hired for this job!

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.040
I'm an outsider! An outsider!

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.410
A woman named Elaine hired me!

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.660
That's a lie!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.370
I'm not lying. This hurts.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:00.750
Take it out!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.620
You said "again" earlier...

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:08.540
She hired me to kill that
rich lady and you! Elaine did!

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.830
Did you hear me? Hey, this hurts a lot!

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:18.040
Elaine was the one who did this!

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.290
Why did Elaine lie?

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.410
You were used.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:47.620
She probably wanted to blame
Dominic's death on Mary's ghost.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.410
Dominic was trying to go to the police.

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:53.000
She must have wanted to quiet her.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.330
Hey!

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:09.250
Annabella. What's wrong?

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:13.200
Dominic is dead. I got rid of the culprit.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.250
Huh?

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:17.410
You were the one who stole this.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.700
What a dirty woman. Full of lies.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.830
Do you have proof?

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.160
I don't need such a thing.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:30.080
Why did you kill Mary?

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.040
It wasn't me.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.450
True. The one who killed her
was that bowling man.

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:40.040
But the people I hate most are the ones
who refuse to get their own hands dirty.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:44.540
You had Dominic and the bowling man dance
in your palm as you stood in the shadows.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:48.910
You showed tears of sadness for Mary.
What were you trying to accomplish?

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:55.160
Dominic was rich. She was useful, right?

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.330
That's why I let her live.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:01.950
But Mary... Her positivity pissed me off!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.830
Her smile was so annoying!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:06.290
She was so honest that I hated her!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.750
Even though she was your friend?

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.250
She wasn't my friend.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.580
Liar!

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:15.750
Don't come any closer! You ugly monster!

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:28.160
That woman is the culprit
behind Mary Russell's murder.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.370
You called me here for that...?

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:35.330
We got statements from her friends.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:39.620
Elaine was the one who pushed everyone
back to Upper during the bravery test.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:44.200
The ones who heard Mary went missing
took an oath to keep it a secret.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:49.040
It was like she was killed
by her own classmates.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.410
The people of Upper really piss me off.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:03.870
Why did you take her face?

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:22.200
"Help me. I don't want to die."
Over and over.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:26.040
I thought that's what it was to be human.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:30.330
I'm glad to know what kind of girl
she was and that I took this face.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.750
She had a dream.

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:35.080
Just like us.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:36.910
Why are you laughing?

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:38.580
No reason.

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.410
There he goes again!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.870
He's drawing Annie!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.160
Hey, Annie!

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:55.790
Look, Annie!

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:59.000
She's in a bad mood.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.330
Isn't it your fault?

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:02.040
Why is it my fault?!

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:06.580
Aw, jeez. So creepy!

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:08.750
He's overflowing with hearts.

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:13.500
People who can't lie put me at ease.

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:15.200
Huh?

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.370
You can draw me from the front next time.
